id: pm-csv-rssj
title: Extend measured coverage to every executable TypeScript script
description: "The 2026-09-28 release gate reports 100% lines, branches, and functions over only index.ts and scripts/docstring-gate.ts. The gate treats V8 line coverage as its statement-coverage figure; it does not emit a separate statements field. This repository has eight scripts/*.ts files plus index.ts. The current 100% receipt cannot support an all-source 100/100/100/100 claim because seven executable scripts are outside the measured source set. Expand the gate without exclusions or artificial counters, and document the line-to-statement mapping precisely."
type: Issue
status: open
priority: 1
tags: []
created_at: "2026-09-28T15:38:07.333Z"
updated_at: "2026-09-28T15:49:00.292Z"
author: codex
acceptance_criteria: "Fail closed if any executable TypeScript file is missing from the coverage report; Report and enforce 100% statements, branches, functions, and lines for all executable source"
severity: high
repro_steps: "Run npm run coverage; observe coverage-gate: 2 source files reported and three dimensions, then compare with scripts/*.ts and index.ts."
expected_result: "Every executable TypeScript source is included in the report and enforced at 100% lines, branches, and functions, with the V8 line-as-statement mapping documented precisely."
actual_result: "2 of 9 executable TypeScript source files reported; line coverage represents statements in this Node/V8 gate, but seven scripts are outside the measured set."
component: quality-gates
body: ""
